<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brasília</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brasília is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, built on the central plateau and inaugurated on 21 April 1960 under President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juscelino-kubitschek">Juscelino Kubitschek</a>. It was planned by Lúcio Costa, with major buildings by Oscar Niemeyer, to move government away from the coast and open up the interior. Its modernist plan is a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brasilia.jpg" alt="Brasília" width="320" height="153" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arturdiasr · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Planalto_Central_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
